flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a lock file of pip-compile fixes itself
    accDescr: A pull request changes a source, such as requirements-dev.in. The step Lock files match their sources has uv compile each lock file again, on a copy, for the Python of its header and on the versions that it pins, and compares the pins. Without a difference, the file stays as it is, also after a new release upstream. With one, the check fails, and the autofix keeps the result below the header of the file; the fix bot commits it, and the checks run again. When uv finds no solution, nothing changes, and the log says why.

    change(["A pull request changes a source,<br>such as requirements-dev.in"])
    compile["uv compiles each lock file again, on a copy:<br>for the Python of its header,<br>on the versions that it pins"]
    differs{"Do the pins differ?"}
    solution{"Did uv find a solution?"}
    kept(["The file stays as it is,<br>also after a new release upstream"])
    failed["The check fails, and the autofix keeps the result<br>below the header of the file"]
    bot["The fix bot commits it,<br>and the checks run again"]
    green(["Every check passes"])
    person(["Nothing changes, and the log says why:<br>a person corrects the sources"])

    change --> compile --> solution
    solution -- "yes" --> differs
    solution -- "no" --> person
    differs -- "no" --> kept
    differs -- "yes" --> failed --> bot --> green

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class compile,differs,solution,failed,bot bot
    class change,person person
    class kept,green done
